cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on its results, please cite the version you used."
type: software
title: "Adding a Thai N-gram Engram to Qwen3-ASR-0.6B: quality, memory, and latency of BF16, NF4, and LLM.int8 inference on ROCm"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation package that adds a token-level bigram/trigram memory (Engram) to a
  frozen Qwen3-ASR-0.6B and measures Thai transcription quality on a fixed
  300-clip held-out set, then compares BF16, bitsandbytes NF4, and bitsandbytes
  LLM.int8 for quality, model-tensor storage, peak allocated VRAM, and latency on
  an AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT under ROCm. Engram step 750 in BF16 reduced corpus
  character error rate from 17.8051% to 9.0448% on this slice; both quantized
  variants were slower per clip than their BF16 counterpart, and Engram NF4
  remained 3.1128 CER percentage points above the BF16 baseline. The deposit
  contains the library, one script per reported result, the frozen evaluation-set
  manifest, the four Engram checkpoints, and every prediction and summary behind
  the reported numbers.
authors:
